my $CODE = <<'END_CODE';
first line
second line
END_CODE

{
    desc => 'P pastes yanked text before cursor',
    description => <<'END_DESC',
Macro: `xt/visual/macros/paste_before_P`

Tests `yy` followed by `P` which yanks the current line then pastes it
**above** the current line.

**initial.png** — Two lines of text. Cursor at line 1 col 0.

Keys: `j` to move to line 2, then `yyP`

**on_line2.png** — Cursor moved to line 2 (`second line`).

**after_P.png** — Line 2 (`second line`) is duplicated **above** itself.
Buffer now has 3 lines: `first line`, `second line`, `second line`.
END_DESC
    run => sub {
        my ($ctx) = @_;
        $ctx->buffer->set_text($CODE);
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('j');
        $ctx->delay(50);
        $ctx->snapshot('on_line2');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('yyP');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_P');
    },
}
